# 32. Set vs List

| Feature                  | List               | Set               |
| ------------------------ | ------------------ | ----------------- |
| Syntax                   | `[]`               | `{}`              |
| Ordered                  | Yes                | No                |
| Indexed                  | Yes                | No                |
| Duplicates               | Allowed            | Not allowed       |
| Mutable                  | Yes                | Yes               |
| Fast membership checking | Generally slower   | Generally faster  |
| Main use                 | Store ordered data | Store unique data |

### Example

```python
numbers_list = [1, 2, 2, 3, 3]

numbers_set = {1, 2, 2, 3, 3}

print(numbers_list)
print(numbers_set)
```

Output:

```text
[1, 2, 2, 3, 3]
{1, 2, 3}
```

