# 33. Real-World Applications of Sets

Sets are useful in many real-world programming situations.

### 1. Removing Duplicate Data

```python
emails = ["a@gmail.com", "b@gmail.com", "a@gmail.com"]

unique_emails = set(emails)

print(unique_emails)
```

### 2. Finding Common Users

```python
website_a_users = {"Rahul", "Vikas", "Arun"}
website_b_users = {"Arun", "Kiran", "Rahul"}

common_users = website_a_users.intersection(website_b_users)

print(common_users)
```

### 3. Comparing Skills

```python
required = {"Python", "SQL", "Linux"}

my_skills = {"Python", "Linux", "Git", "SQL"}

print(required.issubset(my_skills))
```

### 4. Finding Unique Products

```python
products = ["Laptop", "Mouse", "Laptop", "Keyboard", "Mouse"]

unique_products = set(products)

print(unique_products)
```

### 5. Finding Differences

```python
old_users = {"Rahul", "Vikas", "Arun"}
new_users = {"Rahul", "Vikas", "Kiran"}

new_users_only = new_users.difference(old_users)

print(new_users_only)
```

