# 36. Mini Project: Student Skill Analyzer

Create a simple program that compares the skills of students.

```python
student1 = {"Python", "Linux", "Git", "SQL"}
student2 = {"Python", "Java", "Git", "HTML"}

common_skills = student1.intersection(student2)
student1_only = student1.difference(student2)
student2_only = student2.difference(student1)
all_skills = student1.union(student2)

print("Common Skills:", common_skills)
print("Student 1 Only:", student1_only)
print("Student 2 Only:", student2_only)
print("All Skills:", all_skills)
```

This demonstrates how sets can be used in a real-world skill comparison system.

